.TH "CSSUNITVALUE.CSSUNITVALUE" "3JS" "August 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSUnitValue.CSSUnitValue \- CSSUnitValue: CSSUnitValue() constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSUnitValue()\f[B]\f[R] constructor creates a new
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] object which returns a new
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] object which represents values that contain a
single unit type.
For example, \(lq42px\(rq would be represented by a
\f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new CSSUnitValue(value, unit)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]value\f[R]
A number indicating the number of units.
.TP
\f[B]unit\f[R]
A string indicating the type of unit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
The following shows a method of creating a \f[CR]CSSPositionValue\f[R]
from individual \f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] constructors.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]let\f[R] pos = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSPositionValue(
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSUnitValue(5, \(dqpx\(dq),
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSUnitValue(10, \(dqpx\(dq),
);
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue.unit\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue.value\f[R]
